    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** carries our highest projection against a favorable matchup with Liberatore, benefiting from a soft xERA and a potent batting order slot. Meanwhile, **Cole Carrigg** is the day's standout value play; his combination of a hitter-friendly park and a generous xERA for Lugo allows him to eclipse his base projection significantly. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a lock despite facing a tough arm in Wheeler; his elite ability to exploit park factors and his favorable platoon status ensure he clears the 60-point threshold comfortably, even with the inherent risk of a high-tier pitcher on the mound.\n\nSpeed remains our primary strategic lever, and we are maximizing that today with **Nasim Nunez** (64.27) and **Andy Pages** (63.49). **Nasim Nunez** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the opponent's xERA, while **Andy Pages** is projected to thrive against the slow delivery of Bennett, which provides a tangible edge for stolen base opportunities. On the cusp of the lineup, **Luis Lara** was our most difficult exclusion (50.27); he narrowly missed the cut because the current efficiency ratings of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014despite their own platoon challenges\u2014offered a higher composite floor for this specific slate.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup fluidity for our outfield contingent. Both **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** carry the \"Lineup Pending\" tag, which introduces a slight risk to their projected volume. **Kyle Tucker** (62.56) remains a strong play regardless, but we have opted to bench **Wade Meckler** (38.40) and **Denzer Guzman** (31.84) entirely, as both fell well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to the daunting task of facing Misiorowski. We are comfortable with these assignments; the objective today is to balance the 